{"schemaVersion":1,"generatedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","id":"c16639b694a8e8f9f8e32779","canonicalUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260814100719.9548-1-hardikprakash.official%40gmail.com/","channels":["linux-i2c"],"thread":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"thread:lore-git:20260814100719.9548-1-hardikprakash.official@gmail.com","source":{"kind":"static-generated","canonicalThreadUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260814100719.9548-1-hardikprakash.official%40gmail.com/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","contentDigest":"lore-git:20260814100719.9548-1-hardikprakash.official@gmail.com"},"subject":"[PATCH] Revert \"i2c: designware: defer probe if child GpioInt controllers are not bound\"","messages":{"20260814100719.9548-1-hardikprakash.official@gmail.com":{"id":"20260814100719.9548-1-hardikprakash.official@gmail.com","messageId":"20260814100719.9548-1-hardikprakash.official@gmail.com","references":[],"missingAncestorIds":[],"author":{"name":"Hardik Prakash","address":"hardikprakash.official@gmail.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"","address":"linux-i2c@vger.kernel.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"","address":"linux-gpio@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"wsa@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"andriy.shevchenko@intel.com"},{"name":"","address":"mario.limonciello@amd.com"},{"name":"","address":"brgl@bgdev.pl"},{"name":"","address":"basavaraj.natikar@amd.com"},{"name":"","address":"linusw@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"nathan@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"chaitanya.kumar.borah@intel.com"},{"name":"","address":"andi.shyti@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux@leemhuis.info"},{"name":"","address":"regressions@leemhuis.info"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"Hardik Prakash","address":"hardikprakash.official@gmail.com"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-14T10:07:19.000Z","iso":"2026-08-14T10:07:19.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"[PATCH] Revert \"i2c: designware: defer probe if child GpioInt controllers are not bound\"","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"This reverts commit 0a4bb2abc3e56d7be6e69b050c88ba52c87e22bf."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The reverted commit causes a regression on ThinkPad T14s Gen 4 (AMD):\nthe touchpad's I2C controller fails with lost arbitration errors,\nbecause it delays i2c-designware's probe by roughly 500ms, which\nshifts the touchpad's first HID descriptor fetch into a window where\nthe platform's embedded controller is still acting as a secondary I2C\nbus master. Debug tracing confirms the GpioInt dependency check itself\nbehaves correctly (it defers appropriately and confirms the GPIO\ncontroller is bound); the arbitration failure happens roughly a\nsecond after the check passes, when i2c_hid_acpi's own probe attempts\nits first transaction."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The original fix is still needed for the Lenovo Yoga 7 14AGP11\ntouchscreen race the commit addressed, but a corrected version will\nbe resubmitted once the EC bus-mastering interaction is understood\nand handled properly, rather than reintroducing a different\nregression on more widely-used ThinkPad hardware in the meantime."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Reported-by: Thorsten Leemhuis <linux@leemhuis.info>"},{"kind":"code","text":"Closes: https://lore.kernel.org/all/b4a4eadb-282f-464c-843a-19d415a34d0c@leemhuis.info/"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Signed-off-by: Hardik Prakash <hardikprakash.official@gmail.com>"},{"kind":"patch","patchId":"patch:20260814100719.9548-1-hardikprakash.official@gmail.com:0:0"}],"patchIds":["patch:20260814100719.9548-1-hardikprakash.official@gmail.com:0:0"],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[]},"ba1fe2d7-ac65-4665-82cc-43800fa9ed12@leemhuis.info":{"id":"ba1fe2d7-ac65-4665-82cc-43800fa9ed12@leemhuis.info","messageId":"ba1fe2d7-ac65-4665-82cc-43800fa9ed12@leemhuis.info","references":["20260814100719.9548-1-hardikprakash.official@gmail.com"],"missingAncestorIds":[],"author":{"name":"Thorsten Leemhuis","address":"linux@leemhuis.info"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"","address":"andi.shyti@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-i2c@vger.kernel.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"","address":"linux-gpio@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"wsa@kernel.org"},{"name":"Hardik Prakash","address":"hardikprakash.official@gmail.com"},{"name":"","address":"andriy.shevchenko@intel.com"},{"name":"","address":"mario.limonciello@amd.com"},{"name":"","address":"brgl@bgdev.pl"},{"name":"","address":"basavaraj.natikar@amd.com"},{"name":"","address":"linusw@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"nathan@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"chaitanya.kumar.borah@intel.com"},{"name":"","address":"regressions@leemhuis.info"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-14T10:49:54.000Z","iso":"2026-08-14T10:49:54.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH] Revert \"i2c: designware: defer probe if child GpioInt controllers are not bound\"","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On 8/14/26 12:07, Hardik Prakash wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"This reverts commit 0a4bb2abc3e56d7be6e69b050c88ba52c87e22bf."}],"lineCount":1,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"@Andi Shyti, would be great if you could pick this up and send it to\nLinus for 7.2 (aka soon) or ask him to apply this from here. But from a\nquick search on lore it looks like you are busy, on vacation, or\nsomething. No worries, but therefore I might ask Linus to pull this\ndirectly tomorrow to ensure this makes it into 7.2, as mentioned\nyesterday already here:\nhttps://lore.kernel.org/all/9095d7c8-92fe-4163-98f8-a53bbcefd6cb@leemhuis.info/"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"The reverted commit causes a regression on ThinkPad T14s Gen 4 (AMD):"},{"depth":1,"text":"the touchpad's I2C controller fails with lost arbitration errors,"},{"depth":1,"text":"because it delays i2c-designware's probe by roughly 500ms, which"},{"depth":1,"text":"shifts the touchpad's first HID descriptor fetch into a window where"},{"depth":1,"text":"the platform's embedded controller is still acting as a secondary I2C"},{"depth":1,"text":"bus master. Debug tracing confirms the GpioInt dependency check itself"},{"depth":1,"text":"behaves correctly (it defers appropriately and confirms the GPIO"},{"depth":1,"text":"controller is bound); the arbitration failure happens roughly a"},{"depth":1,"text":"second after the check passes, when i2c_hid_acpi's own probe attempts"},{"depth":1,"text":"its first transaction."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"The original fix is still needed for the Lenovo Yoga 7 14AGP11"},{"depth":1,"text":"touchscreen race the commit addressed, but a corrected version will"},{"depth":1,"text":"be resubmitted once the EC bus-mastering interaction is understood"},{"depth":1,"text":"and handled properly, rather than reintroducing a different"},{"depth":1,"text":"regression on more widely-used ThinkPad hardware in the meantime."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Reported-by: Thorsten Leemhuis <linux@leemhuis.info>"}],"lineCount":18,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Tested-by: Thorsten Leemhuis <linux@leemhuis.info>"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Ciao, Thorsten"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"Closes: https://lore.kernel.org/all/b4a4eadb-282f-464c-843a-19d415a34d0c@leemhuis.info/"},{"depth":1,"text":"Signed-off-by: Hardik Prakash <hardikprakash.official@gmail.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"---"},{"depth":1,"text":" drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-designware-platdrv.c | 80 ---------------------"},{"depth":1,"text":" 1 file changed, 80 deletions(-)"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-designware-platdrv.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-designware-platdrv.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"index c8a203fff4d1..6d6e81242f74 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-designware-platdrv.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-designware-platdrv.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -8,14 +8,12 @@"},{"depth":1,"text":"  * Copyright (C) 2007 MontaVista Software Inc."},{"depth":1,"text":"  * Copyright (C) 2009 Provigent Ltd."},{"depth":1,"text":"  */"},{"depth":1,"text":"-#include <linux/acpi.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":" #include <linux/clk-provider.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":" #include <linux/clk.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":" #include <linux/delay.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":" #include <linux/dmi.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":" #include <linux/err.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":" #include <linux/errno.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":"-#include <linux/gpio/driver.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":" #include <linux/i2c.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":" #include <linux/interrupt.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":" #include <linux/io.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -132,80 +130,6 @@ static int i2c_dw_probe_lock_support(struct dw_i2c_dev *dev)"},{"depth":1,"text":" \treturn 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":" }"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"-#if defined(CONFIG_ACPI) && defined(CONFIG_GPIOLIB)"},{"depth":1,"text":"-/*"},{"depth":1,"text":"- * Check whether an ACPI GpioInt resource's referenced GPIO controller"},{"depth":1,"text":"- * has finished probing. Resources with no named controller (resource"},{"depth":1,"text":"- * source string) are skipped, since they can't be resolved to a"},{"depth":1,"text":"- * struct device."},{"depth":1,"text":"- */"},{"depth":1,"text":"-static int check_gpioint_resource(struct acpi_resource *ares, void *data)"},{"depth":1,"text":"-{"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tstruct acpi_resource_gpio *agpio;"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tstruct acpi_device *gpio_adev;"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tstruct device *gpio_dev;"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tacpi_handle handle;"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tacpi_status status;"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tif (!acpi_gpio_get_irq_resource(ares, &agpio))"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\treturn 1; /* not a GpioInt resource, skip */"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tif (!agpio->resource_source.string_length)"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\treturn 1; /* no named controller, skip */"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tstatus = acpi_get_handle(NULL, agpio->resource_source.string_ptr, &handle);"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tif (ACPI_FAILURE(status))"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\treturn 1;"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tgpio_adev = acpi_fetch_acpi_dev(handle);"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tif (!gpio_adev)"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\treturn 1;"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tstruct gpio_device *gdev __free(gpio_device_put) ="},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\tgpio_device_find_by_fwnode(acpi_fwnode_handle(gpio_adev));"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tif (!gdev)"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\treturn -EPROBE_DEFER; /* controller not registered yet: abort walk */"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tgpio_dev = gpio_device_to_device(gdev)->parent;"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tguard(device)(gpio_dev);"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tif (!device_is_bound(gpio_dev))"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\treturn -EPROBE_DEFER; /* controller not bound yet: abort walk */"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\treturn 1; /* bound, skip adding to resource list, continue walk */"},{"depth":1,"text":"-}"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":"-static int check_child_gpioint(struct acpi_device *adev, void *data)"},{"depth":1,"text":"-{"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tLIST_HEAD(res_list);"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tint ret;"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tret = acpi_dev_get_resources(adev, &res_list, check_gpioint_resource, NULL);"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tif (ret < 0)"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\treturn ret;"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tacpi_dev_free_resource_list(&res_list);"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\treturn 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":"-}"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":"-static int i2c_dw_check_gpio_dependencies(struct device *dev)"},{"depth":1,"text":"-{"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tstruct acpi_device *adev;"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tadev = ACPI_COMPANION(dev);"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tif (!adev)"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\treturn 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\treturn acpi_dev_for_each_child(adev, check_child_gpioint, NULL);"},{"depth":1,"text":"-}"},{"depth":1,"text":"-#else"},{"depth":1,"text":"-static int i2c_dw_check_gpio_dependencies(struct device *dev)"},{"depth":1,"text":"-{"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\treturn 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":"-}"},{"depth":1,"text":"-#endif /* CONFIG_ACPI && CONFIG_GPIOLIB */"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":" static int dw_i2c_plat_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)"},{"depth":1,"text":" {"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tu32 flags = (uintptr_t)device_get_match_data(&pdev->dev);"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -214,10 +138,6 @@ static int dw_i2c_plat_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tstruct dw_i2c_dev *dev;"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tint irq, ret;"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tret = i2c_dw_check_gpio_dependencies(device);"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tif (ret)"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\treturn ret;"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tirq = platform_get_irq_optional(pdev, 0);"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tif (irq == -ENXIO)"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\tflags |= ACCESS_POLLING;"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"base-commit: 3d6d817622b0a9721e3cc404df3469171582be13"}],"lineCount":119,"maximumDepth":1}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":1,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260814100719.9548-1-hardikprakash.official@gmail.com","parentId":"20260814100719.9548-1-hardikprakash.official@gmail.com"},"cda84d69-89d2-46f6-9c86-a758bf385f54@kernel.org":{"id":"cda84d69-89d2-46f6-9c86-a758bf385f54@kernel.org","messageId":"cda84d69-89d2-46f6-9c86-a758bf385f54@kernel.org","references":["20260814100719.9548-1-hardikprakash.official@gmail.com"],"missingAncestorIds":[],"author":{"name":"Mario Limonciello","address":"superm1@kernel.org"},"replyTo":[],"